From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:40:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 126/342] meson_vdec: the end of the stream once the firmware
 has frames to decode into

AV_SCRATCH_E did not show the firmware waiting for frames at 1080p; the
driver's own count does: no report waiting for the caller, at most four
frames with the caller.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../kernel/drivers/video/meson_vdec/meson_vdec.cpp    | 11 ++++++-----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/video/meson_vdec/meson_vdec.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/video/meson_vdec/meson_vdec.cpp
index 566afa61f8..fb98e99213 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/video/meson_vdec/meson_vdec.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/video/meson_vdec/meson_vdec.cpp
@@ -1015,9 +1015,10 @@ MesonVdec::_Write(const uint8* userData, size_t size)
 /*!	A sequence end code, for the firmware to put out the frames it holds.
 	Sent while the firmware still decodes, it lost the pictures it had not
 	reported yet (the third from the end; more while it waited for frames
-	back), so it waits until the firmware has been quiet for a while and
-	isn't waiting for a frame (AV_SCRATCH_E): it has decoded what it can
-	(the caller has to take and give back frames meanwhile).
+	back), so it waits until the firmware has been quiet for a while with
+	enough frames to decode into (none of its reports waiting for the
+	caller, at most four frames with the caller): it has decoded what it
+	can. The caller has to take and give back frames meanwhile.
 */
 status_t
 MesonVdec::_EndOfStream()
@@ -1029,9 +1030,9 @@ MesonVdec::_EndOfStream()
 		InterruptsSpinLocker locker(fStateLock);
 		_CheckDecoder();
 		bigtime_t quiet = system_time() - fLastReport;
-		bool waiting = _Dos(AV_SCRATCH_E) != 0;
+		bool starved = fQueueCount > 0 || __builtin_popcount(fHeld) > 4;
 		locker.Unlock();
-		if (quiet > 40000 && !waiting)
+		if (quiet > 40000 && !starved)
 			break;
 		snooze(kPollInterval);
 	}
